\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Detailed Description\par
\pard\plain 
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Logging interface. \par
}{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
The default logging function of the fluidsynth prints its messages to the stderr. The synthesizer uses five level of messages: {\b FLUID_PANIC}, {\b FLUID_ERR}, {\b FLUID_WARN}, {\b FLUID_INFO}, and {\b FLUID_DBG}.\par
A client application can install a new log function to handle the messages differently. In the following example, the application sets a callback function to display {\b FLUID_PANIC} messages in a dialog, and ignores all other messages by setting the log function to NULL:\par
DOCME (formatting) fluid_set_log_function(FLUID_PANIC, show_dialog, (void*) root_window); fluid_set_log_function(FLUID_ERR, NULL, NULL); fluid_set_log_function(FLUID_WARN, NULL, NULL); fluid_set_log_function(FLUID_DBG, NULL, NULL); \par
}}
