{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
SoundFont plugins. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
It is possible to add new SoundFont loaders to the synthesizer. The API uses a couple of "interfaces" (structures with callback functions): fluid_sfloader_t, fluid_sfont_t, and fluid_preset_t.\par
To add a new SoundFont loader to the synthesizer, call {\b fluid_synth_add_sfloader()} and pass a pointer to an fluid_sfloader_t structure. The important callback function in this structure is "load", which should try to load a file and returns a fluid_sfont_t structure, or NULL if it fails.\par
The fluid_sfont_t structure contains a callback to obtain the name of the soundfont. It contains two functions to iterate though the contained presets, and one function to obtain a preset corresponding to a bank and preset number. This function should return an fluid_preset_t structure.\par
The fluid_preset_t structure contains some functions to obtain information from the preset (name, bank, number). The most important callback is the noteon function. The noteon function should call {\b fluid_synth_alloc_voice()} for every sample that has to be played. {\b fluid_synth_alloc_voice()} expects a pointer to a fluid_sample_t structure and returns a pointer to the opaque fluid_voice_t structure. To set or increments the values of a generator, use fluid_voice_gen_\{set,incr\}. When you are finished initializing the voice call {\b fluid_voice_start()} to start playing the synthesis voice. \par
}{\par
