{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Embedded synthesizer. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
You create a new synthesizer with {\b new_fluid_synth()} and you destroy if with {\b delete_fluid_synth()}. Use the settings structure to specify the synthesizer characteristics.\par
You have to load a SoundFont in order to hear any sound. For that you use the {\b fluid_synth_sfload()} function.\par
You can use the audio driver functions described below to open the audio device and create a background audio thread.\par
The API for sending MIDI events is probably what you expect: {\b fluid_synth_noteon()}, {\b fluid_synth_noteoff()}, ... Creates a new synthesizer object.\par
Creates a new synthesizer object. As soon as the synthesizer is created, it will start playing. \par
